# ⚠️ LF EVERYWHERE, OR CI TESTS THE WRONG BYTES (2026-09-02).
#
# The suite is full of source-text assertions anchored on "\n  }\n"-shaped
# blocks (renderer.js is a classic <script>; main.ts is testable by nothing
# else). The index is LF, but windows-latest's git has core.autocrlf=true, so
# every checkout on CI arrived as CRLF and those slices came back empty — CI
# had never gone green on a deliberate commit, and nobody could tell because
# autosave pushes skip it. `eol=lf` makes the checkout match the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.onnx binary
*.bin binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
